-- statement:
--   # Adic congruences, adic cylinders and division charts
--
--   This file sets up the adic language used by the measure-theoretic part of the development.
--   For an ideal `I` of a ring `R` and an `R`-module `M`, `x ≡ y (mod I^j M)` is `adicCongr I j x y`;
--   the adic cylinders `{y | y ≡ x (mod I^j M)}` generate the σ-algebra `adicCylinderSpace I M`.
--   We then introduce the coordinates attached to a division chart (an `O`-linear equivalence
--   `R ≃ (Fin n → O) × R` inverse to `(z, v) ↦ ∑ zᵢ bᵢ + f v`), the curve ideals
--   `(f + π ∑ zᵢ bᵢ)` they parametrize, ideal atlases and their measures, and the power-basis
--   coordinates of an unramified extension `O[X]/(Φ)`.
--
--   ## Main results
--
--   * `mvPolynomial_zero_null`: zero sets of nonzero multivariate polynomials are null for products
--     of atomless finite measures.
--   * `child_volume_ratio`: the local volume recursion for the children of a tangent pattern.
--   * `colored_subset_count`: the multinomial count of partially coloured maps `Fin Q → Option (Fin r)`.
--   * `division_linear_equivalence`: a lifted basis of `R/(f)` yields a division equivalence.
--   * `division_chart_rank_eq_of_residue_ideal_eq`: division charts with the same residue ideal
--     have the same rank.
--   * `finite_coordinate_cylinder_basis`, `finite_coordinate_borel_cylinders`: on `O^n` with the
--     `I`-adic topology, adic cylinders form a basis and generate the Borel σ-algebra.
--
--   Provenance: `Def_SurfaceBlowupV2_{AdicDigits, CylinderFamily, IdealCoordinates, Normalizer,
--   IdealAtlas, IdealChartSigma, UnramifiedMeasure}`, `Thm_Gen_PolyZeroNull`, `Thm_SurfaceBlowupV2_*`:
--   `algebra_product_congruence`, `child_volume_ratio`, `colored_subset_count`,
--   `common_vertical_exponent`, `congruence_bijection_measurable`, `coordinate_constraint_count`,
--   `coordinate_ideal_in_residue_cell`, `coordinate_module_pi_quotient_length`,
--   `coordinate_remainder_raises_order`, `division_chart_rank_eq_of_residue_ideal_eq`,
--   `division_coordinates_{injective, surjective}`, `division_{data, chart}_same_cell_recenter`,
--   `division_linear_equivalence`, `finite_coordinate_{adic_congruence, cylinder_basis,
--   borel_cylinders, linear_continuous}`.

